      Copyright (c) MrOtherGuy and contributors
      Mozilla Public License 2.0 — see vendor/fx-autoconfig/LICENSE

It is vendored rather than fetched at install time so that installing Spacekeeper
never depends on a third-party repository staying available, and so that the
exact loader being written into the browser's program directory is the one you
can read here.

Updating the vendored copy is a manual, reviewed step: copy the files from a
checked-out upstream commit, record that commit hash in the update commit's
message, and diff against the previous copy before committing. The copy is never
edited in place - a local change would be silently lost on the next update.
